## M2.6E — Creation Engine Editor (NEW MILESTONE)

**Position:** After M2.6, before M2.7 (needs runtime components for preview-in-engine)

**Best-in-Class References:**
- **Creation Engine (CK):** Cell-based world editing, region painting, modular kit browser, navmesh bake (Recast), leveled lists, keywords, dialogue graph, Papyrus scripts, preview mode
- **Unreal Editor:** Retained-mode UI (Slate), actor-component model, Blueprint visual scripting, World Partition streaming preview
- **Godot 4:** Scene-tree editor, GridMap for tile-based worlds, TileSet/TileMap, visual shader graph, GDScript hot-reload
- **Unity DOTS:** Entity-component inspector, Burst-compiled systems, DOTS Runtime streaming
- **Blender:** Non-modal editors, multi-window, property panels, operator search (F3)

**Our Implementation (Custom C++/ImGui, Tailored to Your ECS):**

| Subsystem | Output | Tech Stack |
|-----------|--------|------------|
| **Worldspace/Cell Painter** | `worldspaces/<name>.json`, `cells/<wx>_<wy>.json` | ImGui + ImGuizmo, 16-bit heightmap PNG import, 64m cell grid |
| **Region Tag Painter** | Per-cell bitmask: `BiomeTag\|SocioEconomicTag\|FactionOwnership\|RadiationLevel\|ThreatLevel` | uint64_t taxonomy (256-bit = uint64_t[4]) |
| **Modular Kit Browser** | `kits/<kitName>.json` (pieces + connection points + tags) | Grid/vertex snap, auto-connection preview, group select |
| **Navmesh Baker** | `navmesh/<cell>.bin` (Detour tiles) | **Recast/Detour via vcpkg**, per-cell tiles (64m), off-mesh links (doors/ladders), dynamic carving |
| **Component Inspector** | Live EnTT meta reflection — every runtime component editable | `entt::meta` registration in M1 (see below) |
| **Leveled List Editor** | `leveledlists/<name>.json` (entries + inheritance + chanceNone) | **Fallout 4-compatible algorithm** (exact roll logic) |
| **Keyword Manager** | `keywords.json` (256-bit bitmask = uint64_t[4]) | Single-instruction query `(entity.keywords & mask) == mask` |
| **Dialogue/Quest Graph** | ImNodes → `quests/<id>.json`, `dialogue/<id>.json` + bytecode compile | Custom VM (deterministic, save-serializable, no GC) |
| **Script Attach (Lua)** | `scripts/<name>.lua` — onInit/onHit/onCellLoad/onQuestStage/onDialogueEnd | **sol2**, bytecode cache, type-safe bindings |
| **Preview-in-Engine** | Launch `Engine.exe --headed --editor-preview --world=<path>` via named pipe; bi-directional entity selection sync | Child process + local socket (Windows named pipe / Unix domain) |

**Mod Override Chain:** `mods/<modA>/` > `mods/<modB>/` > `base/` (JSON deep-merge for lists, last-wins for scalars)

**EnTT Meta Registration (M1 Extension):**
```cpp
// In M1 ECS framework — register all components for editor reflection
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(Transform);
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(StaticProp);
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(Container);
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(EncounterVolume);
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(NavmeshTile);
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(DialogueStarter);
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(QuestMarker);
ENTT_META_REGISTER_COMPONENT(ScriptComponent);
// ... all runtime components
```

##### Exit Criteria
- [ ] Load Fallout 3 `CapitalWasteland` heightmap (converted) → paint regions → place kit pieces → bake navmesh → spawn 500 zombies → pathfind works
- [ ] Create leveled list `LL_Raider_Loot` → assign to 20 containers → playtest: loot scales with player level
- [ ] Author quest "Find the Cure" (3 stages, 2 dialogue branches, 1 scripted event) → plays in-preview
- [ ] Build settlement: foundation, walls, turret, workbench → assign settlers → save → reload → persists
- [ ] Mod override: `mods/MyMod/worldspaces/CapitalWasteland.json` changes region tags → loads in-editor + runtime
- [ ] Preview launches in <5s, entity selection syncs bi-directionally <100ms latency

