### ADDITION 4: EXPANDED KARMA + FACTION REPUTATION (Extends M8.5)

**Best-in-Class References:**
- **Gothic 1/2:** Reputation per faction + global "alignment" — NPCs react to both; guards attack if faction hostile
- **KOTOR 2 / Mask of the Betrayer:** Light/Dark side (karma) + Influence (companion trust) + faction reputation — all separate but interacting
- **Tyranny:** Faction reputation (Favor/Wrath) per faction — drives vendor prices, companion loyalty, quest access, ending
- **Fallout: New Vegas:** Karma (-1000..+1000) + Faction Reputation (Vilified..Idolized per faction) — separate but interacting
- **Shadowrun Returns (Dragonfall/Hong Kong):** Karma + Faction + Etiquette tags — dialogue options gated by all three

**Our Implementation (Multi-Axis Karma + Per-Faction Reputation):**

```cpp
// Multi-axis Karma (NEW — replaces single-axis)
struct KarmaAxes {
    int16_t goodEvil = 0;         // -1000..+1000 (classic — helps/harms innocents)
    int16_t lawfulChaotic = 0;    // -1000..+1000 (NEW — follows/breaks laws, contracts)
    int16_t selfishSelfless = 0;  // -1000..+1000 (NEW — shares/hoards, sacrifices/uses)
};

// Per-Faction Reputation (drives reactivity — NEW system, separate from Karma)
// -1000 Vilified → -500 Hated → -250 Unfriendly → 0 Neutral → +250 Friendly → +500 Liked → +1000 Idolized
struct FactionReputation {
    std::unordered_map<std::string, int16_t> rep;  // FactionID = editor-defined string
};
```

**Integration Points (All additive to existing M8.5):**
- M8.5 faction economy ODEs → reputation as state variable in population dynamics
- M8.5-EXT-03 Bayesian trust → `selfishSelfless` axis modulates drift rate
- M11 dialogue VM → `OP_CONDITION karma.lawfulChaotic > 500` or `OP_CONDITION faction.rep["Raiders"] < -250`
- M13-EXT-14 faction radio → reputation modulates chatter tone
- M13-EXT-17 companion barks → `selfishSelfless` axis modulates refusal lines
- M8.6 settlement vendors → reputation gates prices (Idolized = 50% discount, Vilified = refused service)

**Faction Definitions (Editor-Created, Not Hardcoded):**
