### [M11-EXT-64] Branching Quest System (NV-style multi-solution)

> **tags** · ui, narrative
> **tl;dr** · Quests fork via 4 mechanics (fight/talk/sneak/bribe); standing+world-state written per branch.
> **ctx** · Branching Quests -- M11/M8. Part 27 + R84 (NV). Reuses M12-EXT-26 (side-quests) + M13-EXT-60 (SLM generator) + M8-EXT-53 (standing) + M7 (world state) + M12-EXT-44 (natural-start). Each quest template encodes ≥2 solution branches: Combat (KILL), Dialogue (TALK), Stealth (SNEAK), Bribe (BUY). NV proved ~30% of quests have this depth; ZE targets all major hub quests.
> **meta** · depends-on: [M12-EXT-26], [M13-EXT-60], [M8-EXT-53], [M7-EXT-20], [M12-EXT-44] · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
Quests are node graphs with explicit solution branches. Branch weight = `{solution_type, skill_req, standing_delta, world_state_shift}`. Combat requires kill/damage skills; Sneak reads M5-EXT-66 stealth + hearing; Talk reads M2-EXT-22 dialogue; Bribe reads M8-EXT-14/15 currency. Each branch writes standing (M8-EXT-53) + world state (M7) on commit.

##### Math
`std_solve = {COMBAT, TALK, SNEAK, BRIBE}`; `branch_weight[solution_type] *= skill / threshold`; `standingΔ = Σ(choices per faction)`; `world_stateΔ = M7 change-buffer write`

##### Algorithm
Quest node graph with forks; each choice writes M8-EXT-53 standing + M7 world-state delta; no main story (per design) — hubs faction/settlement anchored. SLM (M13-EXT-60) proposes, you curate.

##### Examples
-

##### Failure Modes
-

##### Player-Facing Impact
Every choice matters. The story is yours, not a rail.


