### [M13-EXT-53] SLM Content-Drought Guard

> **tags** · NPC, ai, systems
> **tl;dr** · M13. Monitors SLM-generated narrative output for repetition/drought; injects fresh seeds + bans repeats so world text never goes stale.
> **ctx** · SLM Content-Drought Guard -- M13. Guards the SLM broadcast (M13-EXT-60) and lore ambiance (M5.4 scatter, cited M5-EXT-53) against content drought: when generated text repeats or the novelty pool empties, the guard reseeds and bans recent outputs.
> **meta** · depends-on: [M13-EXT-50], [M13-EXT-60] · depended-by: [M13-EXT-60], [M5-EXT-60]

##### Systems Touched
SLM generation loop: novelty tracking, repeat-ban list, seed reseed on drought threshold.

##### Math
`drought = 1 - (uniqueRecent / window); if drought > THRESH: reseed(seed = Hash(worldState, tick)); ban(lastK outputs);`

##### Algorithm
Every SLM emission (broadcast M13-EXT-60, lore ambiance) is hashed into a recent-window set. A drought score rises as uniqueness drops; on threshold the guard rotates the seed (derived from world state + tick, keeping co-op consistency) and bans the last K outputs so they cannot recur. Prevents the "AI says the same thing forever" failure that breaks immersion in long sessions.

##### Examples
-

##### Failure Modes
-

##### Player-Facing Impact
The world's voice stays fresh for hundreds of hours — broadcasts and ambient lore never loop into nonsense.

