### [M2-EXT-03] Continuous Narrow-Phase Contact Point Query Collector Cache

> **tags** · general
> **tl;dr** · Sits in front of Jolt's narrow-phase query API, deduping redundant raycasts/sweeps fired by multiple systems in the same frame — melee parry ([M2-EXT-29]), A...
> **ctx** · M2.9-EXT-12 — M2.9 traversal, ballistics & survival physiology.
> **meta** · depends-on: M2-EXT-29 · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
Sits in front of Jolt's narrow-phase query API, deduping redundant raycasts/sweeps fired by multiple systems in the same frame — melee parry (`[M2-EXT-29]`), AI perception line-of-sight (M5.3), vault ledge-analysis (M2.9), and any `SpatialHash`-adjacent query that also needs a physical line trace.

##### Math
`QueryHash = Hash(V_origin ⊕ V_destination)`

##### Algorithm
Hashes the start/end vectors of a line/capsule query. If an identical query (same origin, same destination, same frame) was already dispatched this frame, the cache returns the cached hit result instead of re-walking the Jolt BVH tree a second time. Cleared at the start of every fixed-timestep tick — this is a same-frame dedup cache, not a persistent result cache, so it never returns stale hits.

