### [M2-EXT-78] Immersive Interaction Shell

> **tags** · general, interaction, ui
> **tl;dr** · M2. A single diegetic interaction layer that hosts the radial (M2-EXT-48) AND all minigame overlays (weld/hotwire/lockpick/hack/pickpocket) — no menu pop-ups, world stays live.
> **ctx** · M2.9-EXT-12 — M2.9 traversal, ballistics & survival physiology.
> **meta** · depends-on: [M2-EXT-48], [M11-EXT-60], [M11-EXT-61], [M9-EXT-30], [M9-EXT-31], [M9-EXT-32], [M9-EXT-33], [M9-EXT-34] · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
All context interactions (M2-EXT-24/25), crafting (M8-EXT-02), and the five interaction minigames (M9-EXT-30..34). The shell owns: prompt surfacing (radial), camera framing for the active minigame, diegetic overlay rendering (M11), and fail/retry state. The world simulation (M8-EXT-59, M5) never pauses — threats keep moving during a pick or weld. Inventory access is via M8-EXT-09.

##### Math
Interaction state machine: `IDLE → FOCUS(target) → MINIGAME(type) → RESOLVE(success|fail) → COOLDOWN`. World delta `Δworld` accrues during MINIGAME at the same rate as IDLE (no time-stop). Overlay opacity `α` scales with proximity, not full-screen.

##### Algorithm
When the player focuses an interactable, the radial (M2-EXT-48) offers the context action (weld / hotwire / pick / hack / loot). Selecting one opens that minigame *inside the shell*: the camera tightens on the object, the diegetic HUD (M11) draws the minigame widgets (seam track, loom, pin column, node grid, rhythm beat) as in-world elements — not a separate screen. The player's body stays in the world and can be interrupted (a zombie lunge cancels a weld; a guard spotting cancels a pick). Failure returns to FOCUS with a consequence (spark, noise, standing hit) but no hard game-over. This makes the five minigames feel like one system, not five bolt-ons.

##### Examples
- Player welds a plow (M9-EXT-30): camera frames the joint, seam track overlays diegetically, a zombie lunges → weld interrupted → must re-steady. Tension is environmental.
- Player picks a safe (M9-EXT-32): pin column drawn on the safe door in-world; a faction guard (M8-EXT-53) walks into view → shell aborts, standing drops.

##### Failure Modes
-

##### Player-Facing Impact
Every hands-on moment shares one language. The world never blinks so you can act — and the dead never wait.


