### [M2-EXT-80] Limb Damage & Dismemberment
> **tags** · combat, gore, physics
> **tl;dr** · M2/M5. Melee/ballistic hits can sever or disable limbs; driven by Jolt constraint breaking + ragdoll part masking, not a sprite swap.
> **ctx** · M2.9-EXT-12 — M2.9 traversal, ballistics & survival physiology.
> **meta** · depends-on: [M2-EXT-43], [M2-EXT-40], [M5-EXT-19], [M6.5-EXT-13] · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
Melee/ballistic damage pipeline → per-limb impulse threshold table → Jolt constraint break on the targeted limb joint → ragdoll mask hides the severed limb + spawns a detached rigid body (M5). Outputs `limbState[part]` (intact / disabled / severed) and a gore event for M6.5-EXT-13.

##### Inputs
- `hitPart` (which bone/limb the raycast or melee sweep struck)
- `impulse` (weapon-class × damage × charged-attack multiplier)
- `limbThreshold[part]` (from weapon archetype table)

##### Outputs
- `limbState[part]` ∈ {intact, disabled, severed}
- gore event → M6.5-EXT-13 (debris/particle budget)
- if zombie: sever → immediate threat removal on that limb (leg sever = crawl, arm sever = no swipe)

##### Math
Per-limb break impulse `I_break[part]` from weapon table. If `impulse ≥ I_break[part]` → sever; if `I_break*0.5 ≤ impulse < I_break` → disable (limp/one-arm swipe). Sever spawns a Jolt rigid body at the joint with the limb's mass; main body ragdoll mask drops that limb.

##### Algorithm
1. Damage resolves on a limb (M2-EXT-43/40). 2. Compare impulse to `I_break[part]`. 3. Below half → intact (just damage). 4. Half-to-full → disable (animation state: limp/crawl, one-armed swipe). 5. At/above → sever: break Jolt constraint at joint, mask limb in main ragdoll, spawn detached limb body. 6. Emit gore event (capped by M6.5-EXT-13 budget). 7. Zombie AI reads `limbState`: leg severed → ground/crawl; arm severed → lose melee.

##### Examples
- Player lands a charged axe swing on a shambler's leg: impulse ≥ I_break → leg severs → zombie drops and crawls, no longer a stand-up threat.
- Pistol headshot: disables head → instant down (head is a special case, always lethal when breached).
- Cleaver to a feral's arm mid-swipe: arm severs → attack interrupted, zombie limited to bites.

##### Failure Modes
- Constraint break without masking → limb floats / double-draws. Guard: always mask in main ragdoll before spawning detached body.
- Gore budget exceeded → cap sever VFX to meat-chunk decals, skip particle spray.

##### Player-Facing Impact
Dismemberment makes melee feel decisive: a well-placed heavy hit ends a threat, not just chips health. M-rated, physical, satisfying — no fantasy, just bone and impulse.

