### [M2-EXT-81] Bleeding & Wound Treatment
> **tags** · survival, injury, medicine
> **tl;dr** · M2/M8. Combat wounds cause blood loss over time; bandage/tourniquet stops it, or the player bleeds out. Ties to survival physiology (M2-EXT-18).
> **ctx** · M2.9-EXT-12 — M2.9 traversal, ballistics & survival physiology.
> **meta** · depends-on: [M2-EXT-18], [M8-EXT-03], [M8-EXT-66] · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
Damage events with a `bleed` flag → accumulate `bloodLoss` rate per wound → drains a `bloodVolume` pool → below threshold = unconsciousness → zero = death. Treatment items (bandage, tourniquet, medkit) from M8-EXT-66 stop or slow the rate. Outputs `bloodVolume[0..1]` and per-wound `bleedRate`.

##### Inputs
- wound `bleedRate` (from weapon: blade > blunt; sever > graze)
- treatment item applied (bandage = slow, tourniquet = stop limb, medkit = full)
- time since wound

##### Outputs
- `bloodVolume` (drains while bleeding, restores via transfusion/rest)
- `bleedRate` per wound (0 after treatment)

##### Math
`bloodVolume(t+dt) = bloodVolume(t) - Σ bleedRate_i · dt + restRestore·dt`. If `bloodVolume < 0.3` → stamina/accuracy penalty (M2-EXT-18). If `bloodVolume ≤ 0` → death. Tourniquet sets `bleedRate_limb = 0` but risks limb loss if left > T.

##### Algorithm
1. Wound with bleed flag opens. 2. Each tick subtracts bleedRate from bloodVolume. 3. Player applies bandage (reduces rate) or tourniquet (stops limb bleed, timer). 4. Below 0.3 → visual tunnel/weakness. 5. Zero → death screen. 6. Rest + medkit restores volume.

##### Examples
- Player takes a knife graze from a feral: low bleedRate → bandage in calm → fine.
- Caught in a wire-trap (M8-EXT-23): high bleedRate on leg → tourniquet or bleed out in ~90s.
- Untreated torso wound during a horde: bloodVolume hits zero mid-fight → run ends.

##### Failure Modes
- Tourniquet left too long → limb necrotizes (adds a disability, not a cure). Enforce T timer.
- Bleed rate not reset on bandage re-use → cap applications per wound.

##### Player-Facing Impact
Bleeding turns every wound into a clock. Loot a bandage, or die in the dark. Survival tension without UI clutter — you feel the drain.


