### [M2-EXT-102]

> **tags** · m2.6, system
> **tl;dr** · M2-EXT-102 — M2.6 broadphase spatial-hash cell index.
> **ctx** · M2.9-EXT-12 — M2.9 traversal, ballistics & survival physiology.
> **meta** · depends-on: — · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched

M2.6 broadphase. Maps world AABBs to spatial-hash cells for coarse pair generation.

##### Math

cell = floor((p - origin)/cellSize); key = Hash(cell.x,cell.y,cell.z); pairs = cells overlapping both.

##### Algorithm

Each dynamic/static AABB is rasterized into the spatial-hash cells it overlaps; candidate pairs come from bodies sharing a cell. Cell size tuned to typical object extent so pair counts stay bounded. Feeds the manifold cache (M2.6-EXT-09).

##### Examples

```cpp
uint64_t key = SpatialHashKey(cell); bucket[key].push(body);
```

##### Failure Modes

Cell size too large: pair explosion, O(n²) broadphase cost. Cell size too small: missed pairs, bodies tunnel through each other. Hash collisions in spatial hash: false-positive pairs increase narrowphase load. Origin rebase mid-frame: spatial hash keys invalidate, requires full rebuild.

##### Player-Facing Impact

Broadphase stays cheap and cache-friendly - few spurious pairs, fast neighbor queries.

---


