<!-- From Archive M2 -->
### [M2-EXT-103]

> **tags** · m2.6, system
> **tl;dr** · M2-EXT-103 — M2.6 narrowphase manifold cache.
> **ctx** · M2.9-EXT-12 — M2.9 traversal, ballistics & survival physiology.
> **meta** · depends-on: — · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched

M2.6 narrowphase. Reuses stable contact manifolds across frames to keep stacking/solver stable.

##### Math

for cached pt: if dist(pt, newContact) < thr: keep pt.id; else new id; refresh warm-start.

##### Algorithm

Persists contact points between frames keyed by a stable feature id so the solver warm-starts (reuses last impulse), giving stable stacks and less jitter. Points exceeding a separation threshold are dropped; new contacts get fresh ids.

##### Examples

```cpp
Manifold m = Cache.Get(key); m.ReuseStablePoints(newContacts); solver.WarmStart(m);
```

##### Failure Modes

Manifold cache corruption: stale contact points cause solver divergence, jitter, or phantom forces. Feature ID instability across frames: warm-start fails, stacks explode. Separation threshold too tight: excessive contact churn; too loose: ghost contacts persist. Simultaneous origin rebase + cache flush: entities lose all warm-start data, one-frame stack collapse.

##### Player-Facing Impact

Stacked corpses/objects stay put instead of jittering or exploding.

---


---

