Electric Fence (Base Defense)

##### Systems Touched
M8.6-EXT-28 safehouse + M4 power + M3 destruction.

##### Math
I_shock = V_fence / R_contact;  // R_contact ~= 800 ohm dry, ~200 ohm wet; shock is CURRENT-mediated, not power
if(powered && touched && I_shock >= 0.075f) Stun(z, VF_LETHAL);
else if(powered && touched && I_shock >= 0.010f) Stun(z, I_shock*STUN_SCALE);
draw = watts*dt;

##### Algorithm
Powered perimeter fence stuns/slows zombies on contact, draining generator fuel. Degrades if generator dies or wire cut.

##### Examples
```cpp
if(powered && zombieTouch) {
    float iShock = vFence / rContact;
    if(iShock >= 0.075f) Stun(z, VF_LETHAL);
    else if(iShock >= 0.010f) Stun(z, iShock*stunScale);
}
fuel -= watts*dt;
```

##### Failure Modes

R_contact swing (dry 800 ohm vs wet 200 ohm) ~= 4x current → accidental VF/kill when contact wet.
Stun() not scaled to I_shock magnitude → sub-threshold hits do nothing or over-stun.
Fuel draw not paused when unpowered → drains generator while switched off.
Player-exclusive check missing → player stunned by own fence.


##### Player-Facing Impact
Turn a safehouse into a fort, costs power to keep running.

