##### Systems Touched
M4 PCG + M13 SLM + M11 UI. Generates contextual signage text via a grammar for world flavor.

##### Math
sign = Grammar(prod, seededRNG(locale)); terminals drawn deterministically per seed.

##### Algorithm
A phrase grammar produces signage (shop names, warnings, graffiti) seeded by world-graph node + locale. **Ownership boundary:** M4's grammar is authoritative for structural signage (shop names, fixed warnings) — deterministic per seed, no LLM involved. M13's SLM overlays only *flavor variants* (graffiti phrasing, warning rewording) onto grammar-provided slots; it never regenerates the base names. Output feeds M11 signage and M13's own broadcast strings so streets read as lived-in. Single owner per field: M4 grammar = base text, M13 = flavor overlay.

