### [M4-EXT-107] Compute-Driven Hierarchical Z-Buffer Downsampler *(RECONSTRUCTED FROM CITATION CONTEXT — VERIFY)*

> **tags** · m4.6, system
> **tl;dr** · Compute-Driven Hierarchical Z-Buffer Downsampler *(RECONSTRUCTED FROM CITATION CONTEXT — VERIFY)* — M4-EXT-107.
> **ctx** · M4.6-EXT-06 — M4.6 memory management.
> **meta** · depends-on: — · depended-by: -


##### Systems Touched
M4.6 + M4.6-EXT-05 cull. Builds a Hierarchical Z-buffer on compute for cheap occlusion culling.

##### Math
hzb[m] = min(2x2 downsample of hzb[m-1]); each texel = min depth.

##### Algorithm
A compute pass builds a mip chain of the depth buffer (HiZ). GPU culling tests each draw's AABB against the HZB mip sized to its screen extent, rejecting hidden meshes before the vertex stage.

##### Examples
```cpp
void BuildHiZ(Texture2D z, Texture2D hzb){ for(m=1;m<M;++m) hzb[m]=MinDown(hzb[m-1]); }
```

##### Failure Modes

Codebook too small. Index overflow. Dequantize error. Not integrated.

##### Player-Facing Impact
GPU culls hidden geometry early - fewer vertices, higher fps.
