##### Math
Yield torque `τ_y = k_y·(θ - θ_0)` (bone stiffness k_y, rest θ_0). Fracture when `|τ| > τ_break` (Wilson et al. bone yield ~ 50-100 N·m for long bones, scaled to game). Filter: only apply if `|τ| > τ_min` (ignore micro-stress).

##### Algorithm
1. Each joint computes τ from Jolt. 2. Below τ_min: ignore. 3. Above τ_break: bone fractures → limb goes limp (ragdoll segment). 4. Between: stiffness reduced (sprain).

