### [M5-EXT-89] Kinematic Character Ledge-Locking Coordinate Re-Baser
> **tags** · m5.2, system
> **tl;dr** · Kinematic Character Ledge-Locking Coordinate Re-Baser — M5-EXT-89.
> **ctx** · M5.2-EXT-15 — M5.2 injury & degradation systems.
> **meta** · depends-on: — · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
M5.2 + M2.7. Re-bases character coords when ledge-locking so mantle/vault stays stable at world scale.

##### Math
local = worldPos - anchor; on lock store local; on unlock worldPos = anchor + local.

##### Algorithm
When a character ledge-locks (mantle/vault), its coordinates are re-based to the ledge anchor so the small-scale animation integration doesn't accumulate float error at km world scale. On release, coords re-base back to world. Prevents drift/snap at extreme coordinates.

##### Examples
```cpp
vec3 local = worldPos - anchor; // on lock; worldPos = anchor + local; on unlock
```

##### Failure Modes

Injury severity random. No consistency.

##### Player-Facing Impact
Vaults/mantles are stable everywhere on the map - no float jitter far from origin.
