### [M8-EXT-53] Faction Standing System (NV-style vector + player-founded faction + leader-of-all)

> **tags** · social, systems
> **tl;dr** · Per-faction {fame, infamy} vector (FNV dual-axis); 5 built-in factions (Raiders, Military, Civilian, Infected Horde, **Remnant Military**) + 1 player-founded dynamic faction; player can become leader of ANY built-in faction except the zombie horde; player-founded faction is 6th dynamic entry with its own vector.
> **ctx** · Faction Standing -- M8. Reuses M8-EXT-14 (barter) + M8-EXT-15 (currency) + M11-EXT-64 (branching quests) + M5-EXT-60 (war spawns). Ties to M8-EXT-60 (world-state graph) + M8-EXT-59 (settlement leadership) + M12-EXT-39 (player HQ → faction capital) + M12-EXT-40 (choices write vector).
> **meta** · depends-on: [M8-EXT-14], [M8-EXT-15], [M11-EXT-64], [M5-EXT-60], [M8-EXT-60], [M8-EXT-59], [M12-EXT-39] · depended-by: [M8-EXT-14]

##### Systems Touched
Faction Standing -- extends M8-EXT-14 (barter) + M8-EXT-15 (currency) + M11-EXT-64 (quests) + M5-EXT-60 (war spawns). Each faction owns a {fame, infamy} vector; NPCs read it to decide price/aggro/dialogue. Player leadership (rank ≥ threshold) unlocks perks: quest access, settlement control, faction perks (medic, trader, horde intel). The **player-founded** faction is a dynamic 6th entry — generated via M12-EXT-39 (build HQ) + M12-EXT-40 (choices). All vectors persist via M7 and feed the world-state graph (M8-EXT-60). **The zombie horde is excluded from leadership** (per user mandate) — you can ally with them (M5-EXT-15 cannibal), but never lead. The 5 built-in factions: **Raiders** (chaos), **Military** (order), **Civilians** (survival), **Infected Horde** (mindless), **Remnant Military** (pre-war continuity government, high-tech/low-numbers, ideological foil to Raiders/Militia).

##### Math
`standing[faction] = {fame ∈ [0,100], infamy ∈ [0,100]}`
- `net_standing = fame − infamy`; thresholds: friendly, neutral, hostile
- `leadership_rank = max(fame, infamy) ≥ 80 && settlement_force ≥ threshold` → NPC address changes to "Boss," faction perks unlock
- `player_faction_id = M8-EXT-60.next_dynamic_faction_slot` (6th slot, capped), owner = `player.StableId`
- `leader_of(faction) → quest_unlock(faction_quests), price_discount/nerf, spawn_intel(horde_intel)`

##### Algorithm
On faction-interaction (kill, quest, trade, gift), write Δ to the vector. NPCs sample `standing[faction]` to decide behavior: neutral → standard prices, friendly → discounts + intel, hostile → markups + aggro. Leadership (rank ≥ 80 + settlement force) unlocks: "Boss" address, unique quests (M12-EXT-37), trader discounts, horde intel feed (M5-EXT-10). Player-foundable faction: build HQ (M12-EXT-39) + reach standing threshold → dynamic 6th entry appears; its standing vectors follow same rules; can war with other factions. The zombie horde is excluded from leadership — you can ally with them (M5-EXT-15 cannibal), but never lead.

##### Examples
- Player kills 10 raiders → raider.infamy = 50 → raider traders 20% markup + aggro.
- Player defends settlement 3 times → settlement.fame = 85 → "Boss," quest unlocks, trader joins.
- Player builds HQ in ruins → player-founded faction slot opens → they can recruit + war with others.
- Player sides with Remnant Military → Remnant.fame rises → drone support, orbital strike beacon unlock; Military.infamy rises → Military marks player hostile.

##### Failure Modes
- Vector explosion (too many factions) → hard cap at 6, player faction replaces empty slot.
- Leadership abuse (become leader of all) → each faction's leader perks are exclusive (only one active); switching costs standing.
- Hostile loop (lead everyone hostile) → some quests remain open, world darkens (G-DREAD), no game-over.

##### Player-Facing Impact
Every faction feels you. Help them → they help. Kill them → they hunt you. Lead them → they follow. Found your own → they're yours. Even evil has a path to safety in this world.


