### [M8-EXT-66] Interaction Tool Economy

> **tags** · economy, crafting, interaction
> **tl;dr** · M8. The immersive interactions consume/require crafted tools (welding torch, lockpick set, hotwire kit, datapad, screwdriver) — made via M8-EXT-02, bought via M8-EXT-14/15, lost on break.
> **ctx** · Interaction Tool Economy -- M8. Gives the five interaction minigames (M9-EXT-30..34) a material cost and a crafting sink, tying them into the living economy (M8-EXT-14/15) and survival pressure. Reuses M8-EXT-02 (crafting) + M8-EXT-14 (barter) + M8-EXT-15 (currency) + M9-EXT-30..34 + M2-EXT-79 (proficiency).
> **meta** · depends-on: [M8-EXT-02], [M8-EXT-09], [M8-EXT-14], [M8-EXT-15], [M9-EXT-30], [M9-EXT-31], [M9-EXT-32], [M9-EXT-33], [M9-EXT-34] · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
All five minigames draw tools from the player's inventory (M8-EXT-09). Torch consumes fuel per weld (M9-EXT-30); lockpick set bends/breaks on over-lift (M9-EXT-32); hotwire kit provides a bypass fob (M9-EXT-31); datapad auto-solves one hack node (M9-EXT-33); screwdriver is the basic pry tool. Tools are crafted (M8-EXT-02) from scrap + traded (M8-EXT-14/15).

##### Math
Tool `durability d` decrements per use; `break` when `d≤0`. Torch fuel `f` drains at rate `r_weld·(1/bandWidth)`. Replacement cost `c = base·scarcityMultiplier(M8-EXT-15)`.

##### Algorithm
Before a minigame opens, the shell (M2-EXT-78) checks for the required tool; missing tool → action unavailable (must craft/buy). Using the tool drains durability/fuel; a broken tool must be re-crafted (M8-EXT-02), creating a resource loop that keeps interactions meaningful. Rich tiers (M8-EXT-62) sell better tools (wider windows); bottom-tier scrap tools are fragile. This makes the immersive layer part of the economy, not free verb-spam.

##### Examples
- Player wants to weld a plow (M9-EXT-30) but the torch is empty → must find fuel (M9-EXT-09) or buy a full torch at a trader (M8-EXT-14).
- Lockpick set bends on a gun-safe over-lift (M9-EXT-32) → must craft a new one from scrap (M8-EXT-02) before the next safe.

##### Failure Modes
-

##### Player-Facing Impact
Skills need tools, tools need scrap, scrap needs the world. The immersive layer is woven into survival, not bolted on.

