<!-- From Archive M8 -->
### [M8-EXT-68] Dual-Axis Faction Reputation (Fame/Infamy per Faction)

> **tags** · social, reputation, alignment
> **tl;dr** · Per-faction {fame, infamy} dual-axis vectors (FNV model). No global alignment meter. Fame = helped faction; Infamy = harmed faction. Both axes tracked independently. Net standing = fame − infamy gates vendor prices, quest access, patrol behavior, and faction-specific mechanical unlocks. Both high-fame and high-infamy paths reach all mechanical endpoints (different flavor). 5 built-in factions + 1 player-founded dynamic faction.
> **ctx** · Dual-Axis Reputation -- M8. Implements action-based alignment mandate. Replaces single-axis "alignment" stub. Reuses M8-EXT-53 (standing vector), M8-EXT-14/15 (barter/currency), M11-EXT-64 (quests), M5-EXT-60 (war spawns). Feeds M11-EXT-65 (dread) via |fame−infamy| distance from neutral.
> **meta** · depends-on: [M8-EXT-53], [M8-EXT-14], [M8-EXT-15], [M11-EXT-64], [M5-EXT-60] · depended-by: [M8-EXT-14], [M11-EXT-65]

##### Systems Touched
Each of the 6 factions (5 built-in: Raiders, Military, Civilians, Infected Horde, **Remnant Military** + 1 player-founded) owns an independent {fame, infamy} vector. NPCs read vectors to decide: vendor price multiplier, dialogue tone, patrol aggro threshold, quest availability. Player-founded faction is a dynamic 6th entry generated via M12-EXT-39 (build HQ) + M12-EXT-40 (choices). The Infected Horde vector is special: fame unlocks **Zombie Beacon** crafting (M8-EXT-70) and horde-night Scout-skip; infamy unlocks **cannibalism** (M5-EXT-15) and mutation access. No global "karma" meter exists — alignment is purely the per-faction vector constellation.

##### Math
```python
# Per-faction reputation state
class FactionReputation:
    fame: int = 0      # only increases
    infamy: int = 0    # only increases
    
    @property
    def net_standing(self) -> int:
        return self.fame - self.infamy
    
    @property
    def tier(self) -> ReputationTier:
        net = self.net_standing
        if net <= -200: return VILIFIED
        if net <= -100: return HATED
        if net <= -50:  return DISLIKED
        if net <=  50:  return NEUTRAL
        if net <= 100:  return LIKED
        if net <= 200:  return RESPECTED
        return IDOLIZED

    @property
    def is_hostile(self) -> bool:
        return self.tier <= HATED or (self.tier == DISLIKED and self.infamy > 100)

# Mechanical locks per axis (both paths reach endpoints)
MECHANICAL_UNLOCKS = {
    "Raiders": {
        "fame": ["—"],
        "infamy": ["raider_cache_locations", "fear_aura", "tribute_demands"]
    },
    "Military": {
        "fame": ["supply_drops", "artillery_callins", "gear_requisition"],
        "infamy": ["—"]
    },
    "Civilians": {
        "fame": ["trade_discounts", "safehouse_access", "recruit_quality"],
        "infamy": ["—"]
    },
    "Remnant Military": {
        "fame": ["advanced_tech", "drone_support", "orbital_strike_beacon"],
        "infamy": ["—"]
    },
    "Infected Horde": {
        "fame": ["—"],
        "infamy": ["zombie_beacon_crafting", "horde_night_scout_skip", "mutation_access"]
    },
    "Player-Founded": {
        "fame": ["all_above_for_your_faction"],
        "infamy": ["—"]
    }
}

# Dread contribution (M11-EXT-65): extreme purity in either direction raises dread
dread_contribution = 0.1 * (1.0 - abs(net_standing) / 200.0)  # max at neutral, min at extremes
```

##### Algorithm
On faction-interaction (kill, quest complete, trade, gift, defend, betray), write Δ to the appropriate axis (fame OR infamy, never both for same action). NPCs sample the faction's vector to decide behavior:
- **Vendor price** = base × factionMod(net_standing) × tierMod(socialTier) × supplyMod(regionStock)
- **Dialogue tone** = "savior" (high fame) → "monster" (high infamy) → "survivor" (neutral)
- **Patrol aggro** = baseAggro × (1.0 + infamy × 0.01) × (1.0 − fame × 0.005)
- **Quest unlock** = tier ≥ LIKED (fame path) OR tier ≤ HATED with infamy ≥ 100 (infamy path)

Both fame and infamy paths reach all mechanical endpoints — a warlord (high infamy with Military) gets black-market contacts; a hero (high fame) gets supply drops. The player-founded faction follows identical rules; its vector starts at {0,0} and grows with player actions toward NPCs who join it.

##### Examples
- Player kills 10 raiders → Raiders.infamy = 50 → raider traders 20% markup + aggro patrols.
- Player defends Civilian settlement 3× → Civilians.fame = 85 → "Savior" tone, safehouse unlock, elite recruits.
- Player trades tech to Remnant Military → Remnant.fame = 70 → drone support unlock; Military.infamy = 30 → Military marks hostile.
- Player crafts Zombie Beacon (requires Horde.infamy ≥ 60) → deploys on horde night → horde redirects to beacon.

##### Failure Modes
- Vector explosion (too many factions) → hard cap at 6, player faction replaces empty slot.
- Leadership abuse (lead all factions) → each faction's leader perks are exclusive; switching costs standing.
- Hostile loop (all factions hate player) → some quests remain open, world darkens (G-DREAD), no game-over.
- Infamy path feels "easier" → raise infamy costs (dread, fewer recruits, higher prices) to balance.

##### Player-Facing Impact
No meter. The world sees you through what you've done. Help a faction → they help you. Kill them → they hunt you. Go deep into infamy with Raiders → they fear you and pay tribute. Go deep into fame with Remnant → orbital strikes on demand. Your faction, your rules. Even the monster path has a way to survive — it just costs more in trust.


