### [M8-EXT-70] Zombie Beacon (Player-Zombie Leadership)

> **tags** · item, horde, stealth, faction
> **tl;dr** · Craftable/looted device. **Gated by Horde infamy ≥ 60** (M8-EXT-68). Deploy → emits pheromone/acoustic signature for 60–120s, 15–25m radius, 10-min cooldown. **Only functions during Siege/Breach escalation tiers** of the dynamic horde (M8-EXT-51) — NOT a fixed calendar night. Mutates horde AI priority within radius: moves toward beacon, attacks beacon's target, breaks formation to swarm. **Using it broadcasts player position to ALL factions** (M8-EXT-53 standing hit). No RTS control; beacon = bait, not command. Horde-night only in legacy terms = Siege/Breach tier only.
> **ctx** · Zombie Beacon -- M8/M5. Implements indirect horde influence per "player leads all except zombies" mandate. Reuses M5-EXT-65 (scent/pheromone), M5-EXT-64 (sleeper/screamer alert propagation), M11-EXT-64/65 (stealth/hearing-cone), M8-EXT-68 (Horde infamy gate). Constraint: no RTS camera, no zombie companion, no direct pathing control. Horror-consistent: you're baiting, not commanding. Skill expression = placement, timing, escape.
> **meta** · depends-on: [M8-EXT-68], [M5-EXT-65], [M5-EXT-64], [M11-EXT-64], [M11-EXT-65], [M8-EXT-51], [M8-EXT-53] · depended-by: [M8-EXT-68]

##### Systems Touched
Beacon entity with ScentEmitterComponent (M5-EXT-65) + AudioEmitterComponent (M5-EXT-64 screamer-range). Active only when dynamic horde escalation_tier ≥ 2 (Siege/Breach). Horde AI within radius gains "Beacon" priority target — overrides normal utility scoring toward beacon location. Beacon destructible (HP scales with craft tier). On deploy: broadcasts player position to all faction standing systems (M8-EXT-53) → small Infamy hit with Military/Civilians/Remnant, small Fame hit with Raiders. Cooldown enforced per-player (not per-beacon).

##### Math
```
beacon_duration = base_duration * craft_tier_multiplier  // 60-120s
beacon_radius = base_radius * craft_tier_multiplier       // 15-25m
cooldown = 600s / craft_tier_multiplier                   // 10 min base
hijack_strength = signal_bonus * craft_tier_multiplier    // competes with other signals

// Horde AI priority override (within radius, Siege/Breach tier only):
if escalation_tier >= 2 and dist(horde, beacon) <= beacon_radius:
    priority = max(priority, BEACON_PRIORITY * hijack_strength)
```

##### Algorithm
1. Player crafts/loots Beacon (requires Horde.infamy ≥ 60 + M5-EXT-65 pheromone synthesis + M8-EXT-02 crafting). 2. Deploy action: places entity, starts duration timer, emits scent+audio. 3. Dynamic horde system (M8-EXT-51) evaluates beacon as additional signal source; hordes in Siege/Breach tier within radius redirect. 4. Beacon HP ticks down under horde attacks; destruction ends effect early. 5. Cooldown prevents re-deploy. 6. Position broadcast: all faction standing systems receive player location ping → Military/Civilians/Remnant: infamy += 5; Raiders: fame += 5. 7. Player escapes (stealth M11-EXT-65) or fights redirected horde.

##### Examples
- Horde night (Siege tier): player deploys Beacon on roof across street → horde breaks siege on base, swarms roof → player escapes through rear while horde destroys beacon.
- Player lures Breach-tier horde into Remnant FOB kill zone → beacon placed at FOB gate → horde + Remnant artillery clash → player loots both.
- Player uses beacon to clear building infestation → places beacon inside, exits → horde funnels in → player seals exits, burns building.
- Failed escape: beacon destroyed early, horde re-acquires player via scent trail (M5-EXT-65) → player caught in open.

##### Failure Modes
- Beacon trivializes horde threat → only works in Siege/Breach (already committed horde), not Idle/Scout; destructible; cooldown; position broadcast punishes spam.
- RTS drift → no unit selection, no move orders, no camera shift. Beacon is a thrown device, not a UI mode.
- Infamy gate too easy/hard → calibrate Horde.infamy ≥ 60 (mid-HATED tier); requires sustained horde-hostile actions.
- Beacon ignored by smart horde → hijack_strength scales with craft tier; max tier = near-guaranteed redirect in radius.

##### Player-Facing Impact
You can't lead the horde — but you can *bait* it. A desperate tool for desperate moments. The beacon screams your location to every living faction, so using it is a calculated betrayal of stealth. High Infamy with the Horde makes better beacons; high Fame with the living makes using it costlier. The apocalypse doesn't give you a zombie army — it gives you a way to point the one that exists somewhere else, for a minute.


