### [M9-EXT-32] Lockpick Minigame (Fallout-Harder)

> **tags** · interaction, stealth, systems
> **tl;dr** · M9/M2. Picking a lock is a tension + pin-state puzzle: set each pin without over-lifting; one slip drops the pick and alerts. Harder and more contextual than Fallout.
> **ctx** · Lockpick Minigame -- M9/M2. Player ask: "lockpicking like Fallout but a little harder and a bit different, mostly the same." Fallout 4 style (rotate tumbler, set pins) as the base, with added noise/alert and material-difficulty. Reuses M2-EXT-78 (shell) + M2-EXT-79 (proficiency) + M8-EXT-66 (lockpick set) + M6.5 (hearing) + M8-EXT-53 (standing on caught).
> **meta** · depends-on: [M2-EXT-78], [M2-EXT-79], [M8-EXT-66], [M6.5] · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
All locked containers/doors (M4-EXT-32 POIs, safes, vehicles, settlement stores). Outputs `lockState` (locked → picking → open) and on failure an `alertLevel` that feeds M6.5 + faction standing (M8-EXT-53) if a guard hears. Proficiency widens the set window.

##### Math
Lock has pins `Pᵢ` each with `setPointᵢ` and `shearLine`. Player rotates tension wrench (hold) while pushing pins; pin `i` is "set" when `liftᵢ ∈ [shearLine-Δ, shearLine+Δ]`. Over-lift past `shearLine+Δ` → pin binds falsely → on release, all set pins drop (reset). `alertNoise = f(pinsDropped, material)`.

##### Algorithm
Fallout base: a tension wrench you hold (trigger), pins you push up one at a time to the shear line; each set clicks. Differences / harder:
- **No auto-snap assist:** Fallout highlights the next pin; here the player must read resistance (haptic/audio) to find which pin is ready — less hand-holding.
- **Over-lift penalty:** pushing a pin too far past the shear line false-binds it; releasing tension drops ALL set pins (full reset), not just the last. Punishes mashing.
- **Material tiers:** cheap padlock = 3 pins, wide window; gun-safe = 6 pins, narrow window + a "relock" pin that re-locks if you pause too long.
- **Noise:** each dropped-pin event emits a faint click; a full reset is louder. Guards/NPCs (M6.5) within range turn to investigate; getting caught mid-pick by a faction (M8-EXT-53) drops standing.
- **Tool matters:** a bent pick (M8-EXT-66) has a narrower window; a proper set is forgiving. Broken pick = tool lost, must craft another (M8-EXT-02).

##### Examples
- Player picks a pharmacy safe (M4-EXT-32): 5 pins, reads resistance, sets 4, over-lifts the 5th → all drop → loud click → a lurker zombie outside turns. Resets, slower, succeeds.
- Pro thief (high proficiency): wide window, reads pins fast, opens a 6-pin gun-safe in 20s, noise minimal.

##### Failure Modes
-

##### Player-Facing Impact
Locks are a held-breath puzzle, not a QTE. A fumble is loud in a world that listens — and the safe might be empty anyway.


