### [M9-EXT-34] Pickpocket / Sleight Interaction

> **tags** · interaction, stealth, loot
> **tl;dr** · M9/M2. Lifting items from NPCs is a timing/positioning interaction: stay behind, match their rhythm, grab — get caught and standing drops (M8-EXT-53).
> **ctx** · Pickpocket Interaction -- M9/M2. Completes the immersive interaction set (weld/hotwire/lockpick/hack/pickpocket). Reuses M2-EXT-78 (shell) + M2-EXT-79 (proficiency) + M8-EXT-53 (standing) + M8-EXT-16 (NPC residents) + M6.5 (awareness).
> **meta** · depends-on: [M2-EXT-78], [M2-EXT-79], [M8-EXT-53], [M8-EXT-16], [M6.5] · depended-by: -

##### Systems Touched
Loot from living NPCs (M8-EXT-16 residents, faction members). Outputs `lootGained` and on detection an `alertLevel` + standing penalty (M8-EXT-53). Proficiency widens the safe-angle window.

##### Math
NPC has a facing cone `θ` and a patrol rhythm `r(t)`. Player must be outside `θ` (behind) and within grab range `d` during a "distracted" phase `r(t)∈D`. Detection if `angle∈θ` or `noise>p` during grab. Standing Δ = -k on caught.

##### Algorithm
Approach from behind (M6.5 awareness cone); shell (M2-EXT-78) shows a subtle rhythm indicator — when the NPC is mid-action (talking, searching, turned), a grab window opens. Trigger grab: success lifts one item (ammo, meds, keys) into inventory; fail (caught in cone or too slow) → NPC shouts, standing drops (M8-EXT-53), may attack. Proficiency slows the rhythm / widens the window.

##### Examples
- Player sneaks behind a trader (M8-EXT-14) mid-haggle: grabs a medkit during the distracted beat → unnoticed. Later the trader notices stock missing → standing dips.
- Clumsy attempt: grabs while NPC turns → "thief!" → faction standing (M8-EXT-53) hits, guards converge.

##### Failure Modes
-

##### Player-Facing Impact
The crowd (M8-EXT-16) isn't just scenery — it's a pocket to pick and a throat to watch. Stealth has consequence.

